## Develop

Open the repository in its devcontainer, which has Node 24 and the Go toolchain.

```sh
npm ci               # install the exact packages in package-lock.json
npm run build        # bundle the program into out/cli.js
node out/cli.js -h   # run it
npm test             # unit tests with vitest
{{- if .Standard }}
make check           # what CI runs: format, lint, type check, test, pack
make dist            # the release tarball in dist/
make help            # every target
{{- else }}
npm pack             # the release tarball
{{- end }}
```

## Layout

- `src/main.ts` is the entry point: it hands the command line and the
  process's streams to `run`.
- `src/cli.ts` is the whole program behind it: it parses flags with Node's
  `util.parseArgs`, writes results to stdout and errors to stderr, and returns
  the exit code (0 for success, 2 for a wrong command line). Tests call it
  directly.
- `src/*.ts` are the program's modules; tests sit next to them as `*.test.ts`.
- `esbuild.mjs` bundles `src/main.ts` into `out/cli.js`, the `bin` in
  `package.json`. The name and version the program prints come from
  `package.json`.
